# Benchmark build artifacts — regenerated by crisp-compile / crisp-hoist-cuda on every run.
# Do not check these in.

# Hoist byproducts (metadata + per-kernel generated harnesses).
*.metacrisp
*_CUDA.cu

# Compiled kernels (.ptx / .spv) are regenerable too — but a fallback may be committed for
# machines where crisp-compile is absent, and is re-included by exception below:
#   bench-intel-driver.py  ships the .spv into the oneAPI Docker container
# Everything else is a throwaway artifact.
#
# The four `!matmul/crisp/...` exceptions that used to sit here were removed 2026-08-22: the
# benchmark reorganisation replaced the technique-named chapters with question-named ones and
# `matmul/crisp/` went away with them, so those lines protected files that no longer exist.
# Nothing under matmul/crisp was tracked.  See the note in matmul/README.md if it returns.
*.ptx
*.spv
!reduction/crisp/sum-reduce.spv
